  "question": {
    "text": "Two objects&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math>, travelling in the same direction start from rest. While the object <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> starts at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and object <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> starts later at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>min</mi></math>. The object <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> has an acceleration of <math><mn>40&nbsp;</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>km</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>h</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></math>. To catch <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> at a distance of <math><mn>20&nbsp;</mn><mi>km</mi></math>, the acceleration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> should be",
