  "solution": {
    "text": "According to question,<br /><br />Object <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> starts at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and acceleration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>k</mn><mn>m</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>h</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br />The time taken by object <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> to cover <math><mn>20&nbsp;</mn><mn>k</mn><mn>m</mn></math> will be,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ut</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>at</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br />Where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>at</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br />Here, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>k</mn><mn>m</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>h</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br />and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>k</mn><mn>m</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>20</mn></mrow><mn>40</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>hour</mi></math><br /><br />Time taken by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>hour</mi></math>, because it started after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>min</mi></math>.<br /><br />The acceleration in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math>,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>20</mn></mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>20</mn></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>160</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>k</mn><mn>m</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>h</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></math>",
